#. module: l10n_ar_stock_picking_batch
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_l10n_ar_stock_picking_batch
msgid ""
".. |company| replace:: ADHOC SA\n"
"\n"
".. |company_logo| image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ingadhoc/maintainer-tools/master/resources/adhoc-logo.png\n"
"   :alt: ADHOC SA\n"
"   :target: https://www.adhoc.com.ar\n"
"\n"
".. |icon| image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ingadhoc/maintainer-tools/master/resources/adhoc-icon.png\n"
"\n"
".. image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/license-AGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"   :target: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl\n"
"   :alt: License: AGPL-3\n"
"\n"
"=============================================\n"
"Argentinean Delivery Guides on Batch Pickings\n"
"=============================================\n"
"\n"
"Extends batch pickings to support Argentine delivery guides (remitos).\n"
"\n"
"The whole module is conditional on the batch having a partner\n"
"(``batch_partner_id``, related to ``batch_id.partner_id``):\n"
"\n"
"* **Partner batches** (single-partner) → delivery guides are issued at the\n"
"  batch level (one remito for the whole batch).\n"
"* **Mixed-partner batches** (no partner on the batch) → delivery guides are\n"
"  handled at picking level, as in a non-batched flow.\n"
"\n"
"Main features:\n"
"\n"
"* **Generate delivery guide from a batch**: a *Generate Delivery Guide* button appears on the batch form once it is validated (state ``done``), the batch has a partner and the operation type has an Argentine document type configured. It creates the guide on the first picking and propagates the number and CAI data to all other pickings in the batch. Odoo's *Generate Delivery Guides* button is hidden on these batches.\n"
"* **Mixed-partner batches**: Odoo's *Generate Delivery Guides* button generates one delivery guide per picking.\n"
"* **Generate from the batch list**: the *Generate Delivery Guide* action of the batch list applies the same rule to each selected batch (one guide for a partner batch, one per picking otherwise) and skips the batches that cannot generate it yet. It replaces Odoo's action for batches, which is unbound.\n"
"* **Generate from the transfer list**: when Odoo's *Generate Delivery Guide* action of the transfer list gets transfers of a partner batch, they get the single delivery guide of their batch. The automatic assignment on validation still numbers transfer by transfer.\n"
"* **Batch delivery slip**: for Argentine companies, the batch prints with the Argentine layout (custom header, CAI, AFIP barcode, customer identification, COT, declared value and number of packages), with or without a delivery guide number.\n"
"* **Synchronisation**: the delivery guide number on the batch is computed from its pickings and kept in sync. Editing it on the batch writes back to all pickings (only those that differ are updated).\n"
"* **Picking view, partner batches**:\n"
"\n"
"  - A warning banner is displayed on the picking explaining that the delivery\n"
"    guide is managed from the batch.\n"
"  - The picking-level *Generate Delivery Guide* button is hidden.\n"
"  - ``l10n_ar_delivery_guide_number`` becomes read-only, preventing\n"
"    out-of-sync manual edits.\n"
"  - ``number_of_packages`` and ``declared_value`` are hidden (set at batch\n"
"    level).\n"
"\n"
"* **Picking view, mixed-partner batches**: no UI changes — the picking keeps\n"
"  its native delivery-guide flow.\n"
"* **Declared value**: the batch aggregates the declared value from its pickings.\n"
"\n"
